# This repository is PUBLIC. Everything below must never be committed.
#
# This is the second of three layers protecting it:
#   1. linux/replicate_from_local.sh copies only from an explicit allowlist
#   2. this file, as a backstop against manual `git add`
#   3. the gitleaks pre-commit hook in .githooks/
#
# Run `make hooks` once per clone to enable layer 3.

# --- private keys and certificates ---
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
id_ecdsa*
id_dsa*
!*.pub

# --- ssh / gpg ---
# Ignore the contents rather than the directory: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so `!**/.ssh/config` under `**/.ssh/` could never match.
**/.ssh/*
!**/.ssh/config
**/.gnupg/
*.gpg
*.asc
!**/keyrings/*.gpg

# --- kubernetes ---
.kube/
**/kubeconfig*
**/*kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig

# --- cloud provider credentials ---
# Patterns with an interior slash are anchored to the repository root, so they
# must be written with a `**/` prefix to reach the dotfiles under linux/home/.
**/gcloud/
**/.aws/
**/credentials
**/credentials.*
**/.terraform.d/credentials*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars

# --- application tokens ---
**/.docker/config.json
**/hosts.yml
.claude.json
.claude/
.codex/
.copilot/
.npmrc
.netrc

# --- browser / app profiles (session cookies, saved logins) ---
**/BraveSoftware/
**/chromium/
**/Slack/
**/spotify/
**/Code/User/globalStorage/
**/Code/User/sync/
**/Code/User/History/

# --- shell history ---
.*_history
*_history

# --- generic secret-shaped names ---
*secret*
*.secret
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- local redaction rules ---
# Internal project/service names for redact_jsonc.py. Naming them in a public
# repository would defeat the point; see the committed .example alongside.
linux/lib/redact-extra-patterns.txt

# --- local noise ---
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.bak
__pycache__/
*.pyc
